<!--
  GH-8913: 6502 carry-chain 16-bit addition renders as CONCAT11(CARRY1(...)...)
  https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/8913

  6502 builds a 16-bit pointer from a base table + (index less-than-less-than 1) using the classic
  two-instruction ADC idiom: ADC to the low byte, then LDA #0 / ADC #0 to
  propagate the page-cross carry into the high byte.  The decompiler never
  recognizes the pair as a single wide (16-bit) add, so the carry leaks as
  CARRY1 / 0xNN compare and the result is reassembled with CONCAT11.

  Bytes are the body of FUN_BANK00__92ef (issue attachment 92ef_bad_decomp.xml),
  loaded at RAM:0x0 (the function entry is offset 0 of the raw blob).  The body
  has two cursor_mode paths (3 and 5), each with two carry-chained adds:
    * the FIRST add per path is the RuleCarryElim constant-folded carry form
      ((0xNN less-than x) byte compare);
    * the SECOND add per path keeps the raw CARRY1 intrinsic.

  Pass 1 uses the default carry-chain recovery. Pass 2 explicitly disables it
  and retains the two old carry idioms checked below. The default's exact
  pointer-expression spelling is not a contract: scalar reads may use
  byte-preserving copies instead of typed pointer dereferences.

  The native before/after consumer in kuna_addcarrychain/tests.rs checks
  page-cross carry and 16-bit wraparound independently of that spelling.
-->
